course: dictionary
lesson: 5238
title: Jewish: describing people and things
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Jewish is an adjective. An adjective describes a noun, so it tells you more about a person, a thing or a custom. «Hanukkah is a Jewish festival of lights that lasts eight nights.» Jewish tells you what kind of festival it is: one connected with Judaism, the religion of the Jews.
explain: Jewish has two meanings. It can describe people who belong to the Jewish people or follow Judaism. It can also describe things connected with Jews or Judaism, like Jewish festivals or Jewish food. Always write it with a capital J, like the names of countries.
explain: Use context to check the meaning. «Kosher means allowed by Jewish food law.» The word Jewish sits next to food law, so it tells you the law belongs to Judaism. Try the swap: replace Jewish with "a religion's", and the sentence still makes sense. That means you have understood it.
fact: Jewish is an adjective, so it describes a noun such as a family, a festival or a food.
fact: Judaism is the religion. Jewish describes the people or things linked to it.
fact: «Hanukkah» is a Jewish festival of lights that lasts eight nights, with a candle lit on the menorah each night.
fact: «Kosher» means allowed by Jewish food law, such as no pork and not mixing meat and milk.
exercise: «Hanukkah is a Jewish festival of lights that lasts eight nights.» What does Jewish describe here? | a holiday from school | a type of cake | a bright lamp | *a festival connected with Judaism
exercise: «Kosher means allowed by Jewish food law.» Which word tells you the law is connected with Judaism? | Food | *Jewish | Allowed | Kosher
exercise: Which word is spelled correctly? | JEWISH | *Jewish | jewish | jEWISH
test: Which one is a Jewish festival? | *Hanukkah | Christmas | Diwali | Eid
test: «Jewish families sit shiva, a week of mourning at home.» What does Jewish describe here? | the friends | the food | the week | *the families
exam: What does Jewish mean? | a kind of music | *connected with Jews or Judaism, the religion of the Jews | a type of bread | a place to sleep
